{:task "seon.turn/observe-reads-are-renders", :plan "Owner, 2026-10-27 (approved direction, via root): \"I want the eval system to stay rock solid and for it to be focused on executing code and instrumenting it ... Info that is derived and made for the agent or the user should go into the hiccup ... The whole web rendering only what's changed seems like an opportunity to make expensive ops mostly cheap as you only pay them once.\" What exists: seon.turn/observe (turn.clj) runs every turn: agent/prove! (a blocking test run), added-gaps, branch/unmerged, problems/caused-split, task/task, agent/merge-readiness (99% of a turn: 1.78B ticks with main moved, from seon.merge/touched-keys over main's whole diff), program/divergence and the done rule; basis! stores :observed (results, reasons, will-merge, merge) in :seon.turn/basis (derived data in the db, against the 2026-10-26 ruling), observed! holds it in agent state for my.task/status; run-tests-forked's parent waits for its child (agent.clj, read-to-exit) on the agent's one thread; test-plan reads stored-results on the branch db, where results never land (they land on main). The experiment (root's scratchpad render-not-eval.md, forms 01-16) measured them as renders: nothing moved 108 ticks, an unrelated eval 8K ticks with nothing re-run, main moving re-runs only merge-view; a render's cached output equals a fresh call. Build: (1) seon.render.ui components declaring :seon.db/db, each with main's and base's t (ctx's environment :main-t :base-t, ctx-atom's) as children: merge-view (delta-three-way; child divergence's value until datoms-diff's reads are in its read set), caused-view (caused-split), tests-view (the plan's selection, main's results at its digests, an unrun test shown running), gaps-view (added-gaps), divergence-view; placed in render-ctx's task list beside status. (2) seon.turn/observe keeps only the done rule's inputs, called directly (the judge and hand-back! call the same functions at the run's end); merge-readiness, divergence, :attention, :tests, :reds and the prove! wait leave the turn; basis! stores no :observed; observed!/input become a read of the page and my.task/status reads it. (3) each eval's commit sends one non-blocking :prove; tests-view shows its results from main. (4) (fork f) -> value, its answer a message, never a wait; run-tests-forked its caller. (5) test-plan reads results from main. Deletes: observed, :seon.turn/basis's :observed, the prove! wait in observe, merge-readiness per turn. Proofs: an unrelated eval re-runs none of these renders (ledger :hit, a frame under 10K ticks); a main move re-runs merge-view once; the cached output equals a fresh call; a turn's observe under 15M ticks with main moved (1.78B today); the judge's verdict unchanged on the e2e checks. Owner: agent view (this session), turn.clj and agent.clj's test-run parts by root's go; ctx-atom adds :main-commit and :base-commit. Phase A (this branch): (1) less tests-view and (2); the tests view waits on phase B, (3)-(5), which gives it a producer.", :changed #{"seon.render.ui/gaps-view" "my.task/status" "seon.turn/observed" "docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches" "seon.agent/run-tests-forked" "seon.turn/observe" "seon.render.ui/commit-db" "docs/health.md#a-stale-section" "seon.render.ui/render-ctx" "seon.agent/test-plan" "docs/turn.md#observe" "seon.merge/readiness" "my.agent/deferred" "seon.context/turn-state" "seon.render.ui/merge-view" "seon.render.ui/divergence-view" "seon.agent/merge-main!" "seon.agent/heard-main" "seon.render.ui/caused-view" "docs/agent.md#what-you-read" "docs/health.md#what-a-branch-caused"}, :shown {:sections ["docs/turn.md#observe 55%: Each turn starts from facts measured now, never remembered: `seon.turn/observe` asks the test service (`seon.agent/prove!`, `seon.prove`: one run per branch and tx whoever asks, in a fork of the agent) to run the task's accumulated proofs and the tests the branch changed, each test bounded by `:seon.config.agent/test-ticks` (a run that cannot be made ran no proof, so every proof is unknown and the run's error is `:test-run`), the contract gaps the branch adds since its merge base (`seon.merge/uncontracted`, the question root's judge asks), its unmerged entries, the problems its own work made true (`seon.problems/caused`: it refuses done), and the done rule over them (`seon.reconcile/done-explain`: [tasks](tasks.md#the-done-rule)), read from the reconciler's index of the branch, which the agent holds across turns and observes from the last turn's db over what differs (`seon.turn/index!`, `seon.reconcile/index`): listing it again every turn cost 92M ticks and 384 MB on a main of 680 tasks, observing it 1.3M and 10 MB. That is all a turn observes: the done rule's inputs. What else a reader wants of the branch (whether it can merge, what its merge carries, what it changed under the wiki, its tests) is a view of the task's render (```seon.render.ui/merge-view```, `divergence-view`, `caused-view`, `gaps-view`), a component over the branch's db with main's and the merge base's commits as its children, drawn when one of them moves, never per turn (owner, 2026-10-27: \"Info that is derived and made for the agent or the user should go into the hiccup\"). Merge readiness per turn read main's whole diff (1.78B ticks with main moved); a turn's observe now costs 9.4M ticks (measured on an outside agent, nothing new), and an unrelated eval redraws none of the views (`seon.render-test/an-unrelated-change-redraws-none-of-the-merge-views`)." "docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches 13%: A merge runs what the change reaches, not every check." "docs/merging.md#the-test-service 13%: One proc, `:prove` (```seon.prove/prove-proc```, declared in `resources/seon/system.edn`), admits every request to run tests, whoever asks: a Claude session (the server's `:prove` op, the MCP tool `seon_prove`, ```seon.root/prove!```) and an agent's turn (```seon.agent/prove!```, which ```seon.turn/observe``` calls) share it, so a change is proved once." "docs/storage.md#merges-read-what-changed 11%: A merge decides what merges from the datoms that differ, never by reading whole programs." "docs/ctx.md#kept-by-the-change-never-rebuilt 11%: ``seon.ctx/build`` walks the pattern once, when the agent's state first holds its db (a spawn, a resume, a clone), and ``seon.ctx/patch`` keeps it from each transaction's datoms, which ``seon.agent/transact!`` records with the db they made."], :functions [["seon.turn/act! 5%: One model turn: the context of what was observed to the model, the reply's eval calls through the one REPL path, each answered as its own result, the turn's facts on the branch." [:seon.config.ai/cache-block-tokens :seon.run/id :seon.task/id :seon.turn/basis :seon.turn/calls :seon.turn/error :seon.turn/errors :seon.turn/finish :seon.turn/forms :seon.turn/id :seon.turn/model :seon.turn/ms :seon.turn/n :seon.turn/origin :seon.turn/reasoning :seon.turn/red :seon.turn/reply :seon.turn/run :seon.turn/sent :seon.turn/split :seon.turn/tokens :seon.turn/truncated]] ["seon.context/turn-state 4%: The turn sections of task t's current state as data, measured again each turn from observed: proofs with their status, red assertions, source and calls; what else the done rule refuses (regressions, stray reds, contract gaps), and a test run that failed as a whole; the branch's unmerged entries (base, ours, theirs); what happened to the last reply; turns left." [:seon.task/task]] ["seon.turn/context-block 4%: The request of task as a model is sent it on this branch now (the proofs run again): what an outside agent working the task reads, the system prompt and its page, as one text, recorded as a turn of the run (origin :outside)." [:seon.run/id :seon.task/id :seon.turn/basis :seon.turn/id :seon.turn/n :seon.turn/origin :seon.turn/run :seon.turn/sent :seon.turn/split]] ["seon.problems/caused-split 4%: {:caused :attention :rows}: the derived problems the branch at head has that base (its merge base) had not, by message (:rows: each with its class, both kinds): what the branch's own work broke (:caused: the done rule refuses while any is open, seon.reconcile/done-explain :open-problem) and what it changed under the wiki (:attention: the sections it made stale, which the agent reads and never a reason to refuse; the classes :seon.problems/attention declares)." [:seon.merge/changes :seon.problems/class]] ["seon.render.ui/status 4%: What the newest turn of the run observed, a model's or an outside read's (a component over ctx and the db), as (my.task/status) answers it: seon.context/turn-state over the turn's recorded basis (seon.context/turn-input, with the model turn before it for its last reply), as a call of the one printer (the model reads the data)." [:seon.config.render/value-budget :seon.ctx/ctx :seon.render/opts :seon.task/id :seon.turn/basis :seon.turn/calls :seon.turn/origin :seon.turn/truncated]]], :schemas [[:seon.turn/basis "28%"] [:seon.turn/not-observed "14%"] [:seon.run/run-fact "5%"] [:seon.task/state "5%"] [:seon.db/agent-fact "4%"]]}}
{:task "seon.fx/the-source-tree-follows-main", :plan "Found 2026-10-27 by root (approved the same day; branch jolt/the-source-tree-follows-main, nothing built yet, only this entry). Symptom: the standing root runs main's new binary after every merge, but main's program in runs/store held seon.repl/draw-part (build 3 deleted it) and no vars of seon.ratom, so agents forking from root's main get a stale program, and the page shows problems in deleted code (an unnamed catch site in draw-part, 52 dead citations). Cause: main's program is imported from the write-back tree, not the checkout: config/local.edn sets :seon.config.source/root to .worktrees/merges (branch jolt/merges), and only bin/update's step 2 (git -C .worktrees/merges merge --ff-only main) moves it. The jolt/merges reflog shows that fast-forward on every merge until 2026-10-26 20:04 (4436167591, 'merge-log: a fresh root loads its task files') and none after: that night's merges restarted root with bin/root and never ran bin/update, so jolt/merges stood 262 commits behind main (0 commits of its own). Boot's catch-up (seon.root/import-source!) runs every restart and reads (:root source), the frozen tree, faithfully; the source fact even says so (:seon.root/source :unshared 'the binary was built from tree c4aa40e6..., the source is tree 4bc70d16...'), which nothing reads. The narrowed watch (2e4ae8d360, 20:49) came after the freeze and is not the cause, but there is a second defect beside it: my.root/loader-dirs and the own ref use (config/checkout), the main tree, while the importer reads the source root. So a merge into main moves refs/heads/main and fires a :source load that re-imports the unchanged write-back tree, and a commit in the write-back tree (Seon's own write-back) is not the checkout's ref and fires nothing. Unblocked by hand: root ran bin/update (0 jolt/merges commits to merge, jolt/merges fast-forwarded to main, rebuilt, restarted). Correct, at the cause (root's go, 2026-10-27): the source tree follows main inside the :source effect (seon.fx/read-source, called by seon.root/import-source! at boot and on each :source load). When the write-back branch is an ancestor of the checkout's main, it is fast-forwarded first (through the :git owner, an effect, in the write-back tree). When it holds commits main lacks (Seon's merges not yet in main), it is imported as now and the gap is a recorded problem naming both shas and both counts, never silent. The watch watches the source root's dirs and fires on main's ref and on the write-back branch's ref, so the watch and the import name one tree: loader-dirs' :source from the source root; :docs and :tasks stay the checkout's. Deletes bin/update's step 2 (steps 1 and 3-5 stay). Estimate src +40/-10 (seon.fx, seon.root, my.root, bin/update). Proofs, red first: an e2e on its own clone (as seon.source-test/a-restart-catches-up-and-a-new-generation-resumes builds one, with its own results dir) where a commit to the clone's main that defines a var reaches main's program while root runs (the var's entity is there after the ref moves) and across a restart; a write-back branch holding a commit main lacks is a recorded problem naming both shas; and my.root/watch-loads fires :source for a path under the source root and for the write-back branch's ref.", :changed #{"my.root/watch!" "my.root/watch-loads" "my.root/source-root" "seon.root/import-source!" "docs/failure-points.md#edges-that-catch-each-names-its-one-variant" "my.root/loader-dirs" "seon.fx/follow-main" "seon.fx/read-source" "docs/source.md#import-the-running-generations-source-as-mains-program"}, :shown {:sections ["docs/source.md#import-the-running-generations-source-as-mains-program 56%: At every boot root imports its checkout's source tree as main's program, replacing main's program when the files read otherwise than at the last import; the boot as a whole is [root](root.md#boot). (A root started without `SEON_PROFILE` has no model provider: [model](model.md#no-default-model).)" "docs/health.md#every-writer-root-loads-what-changed 43%: Root watches what its loaders read (the wiki, the task files, the source dirs: `my.root/loader-dirs`) and its repository's refs, never the whole checkout, whose builds, stores and other worktrees no loader reads, so whoever writes (a Claude session, a Seon agent, the owner's editor, git) reaches the same facts with no script of their own (owner, 2026-10-23: \"seon code detecting and updating, not external scripts\")." "docs/failure-points.md#edges-that-catch-each-names-its-one-variant 19%: The failure points whose edge function catches, each with the one variant it declares and who handles it as data." "docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches 17%: A merge runs what the change reaches, not every check." "docs/source.md#mains-program-follows-the-tree 15%: Main's program is the tree's: at each boot, when the files read differently from main's last import (their digest differs from the fact's `:digest`, or none is recorded), main's program is replaced by the tree's in one transaction, ```seon.source/replace-tx```; when they read the same, nothing is imported or written."], :functions [["my.root/watch! 9%: Root watches what its loaders read, loader-dirs (the wiki, the task files, the source dirs), and its repository's refs (seon.watch, FSEvents: every writer, a Claude session, an agent, the owner's editor, git), never the whole checkout, whose builds (target/), store (runs/) and, in the main tree, other worktrees no loader reads." [:seon.root/id :seon.root/sys :seon.root/watch]] ["seon.root/import-source! 7%: Main's program follows Seon's own source (seon.source): root's dirs read through the :source effect (first brought to the main checkout's branch, seon.fx/read-source: fast-forwarded when behind, a recorded gap when it holds commits main lacks; their files, the tree's HEAD commit and its reference-code pins, and the tree's inputs with no program facts, seon.fx/inputs)." [:form/id :ns/file :schema/file :seon.error/message :seon.error/subject :seon.root/id :seon.root/source]] ["seon.root/start! 4%: Boot the control process, the fork server and the root graph on its main, a branch of the one store (DECISIONS, Branches as in production)." [:seon.config.agent/max-running :seon.config.agent/stall-ms :seon.config.ai/max-in-flight :seon.config.ai/rate :seon.config.root/api-writes :seon.config.root/gc-sweepers :seon.config.root/main :seon.config.root/reconciler-buf :seon.config.root/store-path :seon.config.root/system-path :seon.config.root/writer-batch :seon.config.root/writer-buf :seon.config.source/branch :seon.config.source/dirs :seon.config.source/gate-checkout :seon.config.source/root :seon.config.store/backend :seon.config.vector/batch :seon.config.vector/model :seon.config.vector/texts :seon.config.web/port :seon.error/message :seon.root/id :seon.root/previous-end :seon.root/sys]] "my.root/loader 4%: Which of main's loaders reads path (absolute) under checkout co: :docs (a page, .md, under the wiki's dir), :tasks (a task file, .edn, under the task dir, which a test root keeps outside its checkout), :source (under a source dir), or nil: the dirs are loader-dirs, the ones watched." "seon.fx/follow-main 4%: Bring the write-back checkout at base (Seon's own source tree, on a branch of its own) to the branch of the main checkout co: fast-forwarded (git merge --ff-only in base) when its HEAD is an ancestor of it, so the source follows main with no step of the owner's."], :schemas [[:seon.config.source/root "39%"] [:seon.problems/class "17%"] [:seon.config.source/gate-checkout "13%"] [:seon.config.root/tasks-dir "12%"] [:seon.task/state "7%"]]}}
{:task "datahike.db/a-diff-records-its-reads", :plan "Found by root's render-not-eval experiment, 2026-10-27 (blocker 1): d/datoms-diff (reference-code/datahike/src/datahike/db.cljc, datoms-diff) reaches psi/diff past the index protocol (datahike.index.interface), whose -slice, -rslice, -lookup and -count-slice record each range under d/with-reads (di/record-read!), so a read built on a diff recorded nothing: a render over a diff (merge readiness as a render) was skipped after its branch added a program key, keeping its old answer. Fix in the fork (jolt/a-diff-records-its-reads, 65dad766): psi/diff records its [from to] range as -slice does, so the read's key is the diffed attribute ([:a a]) or :any, and seon.render's walk matches a transaction against it like any read (render!, frame!). Coarse by design: any datom in the diffed range touches it, as a slice's does. Replaces nothing; the alternative, a render passing the diff's inputs as its children, is a second way to say what it read. Seen on the way: task a-diff-equals-the-set-difference-on-every-history.", :changed #{"docs/forks.md#jolt" "docs/forks.md#datahike"}, :shown {:sections ["docs/forks.md#datahike 55%: `reference-code/datahike` pinned at `a9df162d`, the tip of ``jolt/own-suites-on-jolt`` (tests only: `a989ac4a` the core suites load on Jolt, `datahike.test.utils`, `api-test` and `core-test` requiring the hitchhiker tree and `kaocha.stacktrace` only on the JVM; `a9df162d` the tests our commits left stale: `query-cache-test` reads a failed call's message as the cause `6b668f0` wraps, `versioning-test` reads the roster through `branches` (`c0f9149`) and names a transaction id past every branch's (`be25be4`), `gc-test` counts the roster's two records, `query-ir-test` expects Jolt's per-cursor merge; [own suites](#own-suites)), on `e8a2999d`, the tip of ``jolt/attr-compare-mixed-kinds`` (`cmp-attr-nil` compares two attributes of one kind, keywords, entity ids or strings, with no `try`, and any other pair through `safe-compare`: a variable attribute bound to a string, long or symbol is a slice bound no stored attribute compares with, which since `cc614f4e` threw `ClassCastException` where it had joined nothing, and Seon's `[?f ?a ?s]` with `?a` an input in `seon.docs` reaches it. Proof: `datahike.test.query-planner-test/test-variable-attribute-bound-upstream-reads-bound-slices`, red since `cc614f4e`, green; 0.7 B a keyword comparison. Generic), on `219f57f6`, the tip of ``jolt/diff-test-on-jolt-file-store`` (Datahike's `datoms_diff_test` requires `konserve.jolt.store`, so its restored histories run on Jolt's `:file` backend: without it every restored history threw on konserve's JVM store and the property reported the throw as a counterexample; the diff was exact; test only), on `416bdc63`, the tip of ``jolt/a-diff-records-its-reads`` (`65dad766`: `psi/diff` records its `[from to]` range as `-slice` does, so a read built on `d/datoms-diff` under `d/with-reads` is touched by a datom added in the diffed range: `[:a attr]`, or `:any` with no attribute; it recorded nothing, and a render over a diff kept its old answer. Proofs: `datahike.test.datoms-diff-test/a-diff-records-the-range-it-read`, `seon.render-test/a-render-over-a-diff-runs-again-when-the-diff-moves`. Generic), merged with `0d6b58c0`, the tip of ``jolt/compare-value-no-try`` (`d4811ddf`, `0d6b58c0`: `compare-value` on Jolt enters no `try` for two values of one scalar kind, 240 B a comparison that reaches the value before; `compare-data`'s helpers are top-level fns: n refs on one form 38 to 17 KB a datom at 1,000, `seon.db-test/a-value-costs-its-index-inserts`; a type test beside the `try` until Jolt's `try` costs nothing entered, task jolt.backend/a-try-entered-allocates-nothing), on `cc614f4e`, the tip of ``jolt/attribute-compare-without-try`` (`cmp-attr-nil` compares attributes with no `try`), on `e5a55664`, the tip of ``jolt/time-pred-order``, on `872bfa03`, the tip of ``jolt/pull-reverse``, on `336de2ab`, the tip of ``jolt/tx-data-retracts``, on `3fe48c96` (``jolt/multival-lookup-ref``), on `6dc9ce64`, the tip of ``jolt/with-reads`` (`6689077e` records the index ranges a read scanned: `with-reads`, `reads-index`, `datom-keys`, `reads-touched?`; `6dc9ce64` the collector is an atom), on `698a2fa`, the tip of ``jolt/a-predicate-that-throws-is-an-error`` (`6b668f0`, `25cc875`, `698a2fa`), on `d89be47` (the tip of ``jolt/datom-cost``: `6db7188` and ``jolt/nested-call-refused`` (`ae35add`, `dda24c0`), each on ``jolt/release-drains`` `bae7c3e` (``jolt/in-scalar`` `1880fcc` merged into it; both on ``jolt/global-ids`` `b4596cf`, ``jolt/gc-cache-epoch`` `700c473` merged in))." "docs/ctx.md#kept-by-the-change-never-rebuilt 17%: ``seon.ctx/build`` walks the pattern once, when the agent's state first holds its db (a spawn, a resume, a clone), and ``seon.ctx/patch`` keeps it from each transaction's datoms, which ``seon.agent/transact!`` records with the db they made." "docs/render.md#reactive-renders 12%: A render reads ctx as Reagent's components read a ratom: ```seon.ratom``` is reagent.ratom ported (`RAtom`, `Reaction`, `run-in-reaction`, `flush!`, `dispose!`; Reagent's own tests, `seon.ratom-test`), with the cursor inferred (owner, 2026-10-26: \"I'd rather infer the cursor than require it\")." "docs/source.md#tests-run-by-reach 9%: A test runs only when something it reaches changed since it was last green, in any checkout (task `seon.program/tests-run-by-reach`)." "docs/turn.md#observe 7%: Each turn starts from facts measured now, never remembered: `seon.turn/observe` asks the test service (`seon.agent/prove!`, `seon.prove`: one run per branch and tx whoever asks, in a fork of the agent) to run the task's accumulated proofs and the tests the branch changed, each test bounded by `:seon.config.agent/test-ticks` (a run that cannot be made ran no proof, so every proof is unknown and the run's error is `:test-run`), the contract gaps the branch adds since its merge base (`seon.merge/un